# This is the .dockerignore Docker actually reads for
# `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .` — Docker only honors a
# .dockerignore at the root of the *build context* (the path argument,
# `.` here), not one sitting next to the Dockerfile. deploy/.dockerignore
# documents the same intent but, for that exact command, has no effect —
# this file is the one that does. .env in particular must never end up in
# the build context at all: excluded here means it's never sent to the
# Docker daemon in the first place, not just skipped by a later COPY.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.sqlite3
.env
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
normalization_output/
tests/
.git/
